* Total Naranjo Score: +7
* Causality Classification: Probable (Score Range: 5 to 8)

#### Detailed Score Breakdown
* Question 1 (+1): Fluoroquinolone-induced tendinopathy and tendon rupture (black box warning) is well-documented in pharmacovigilance databases.
* Question 2 (+2): Clear temporal onset with tendinopathy developing 8 days after starting Levofloxacin.
* Question 3 (+1): Positive de-challenge; contralateral (left) tendinitis improved following Levofloxacin discontinuation.
* Question 4 (0): Re-challenge was not attempted due to severe risk of re-injury.
* Question 5 (+2): Mechanical trauma, severe exercise, gout, and corticosteroid co-administration were ruled out.
* Question 10 (+1): Confirmed objectively via ankle ultrasound demonstrating full-thickness Achilles tendon rupture.

